--- TEST: SYN-009
--- Area: Applications
--- Priority: high
--- Name: env.get of an unset variable raises the documented halt
--- Expect:
---   In 4.4 env.get of an unset variable silently returned an empty
---   string (or 0 under the JIT). The documented behavior is halt.error:
---   the frame aborts, so the FAIL marker at the end is never printed
---   when the fix is in place. A set variable still reads back a value.

s: p = env.get("PATH");

if (p.length > 0) then
    >! "[SYN-009-1] PASS - set variable reads back";
else
    >! "[SYN-009-1] FAIL - PATH read as empty";
end

s: gone = env.get("XCX_DEFINITELY_UNSET_4RC1_QQ");
>! "[SYN-009-2] FAIL - unset env.get returned silently";
